  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Thomas F. Lozick leads Swagelok, the Ohio fluid-systems manufacturer founded by his grandfather, Fred Lennon. Before joining the family business, he owned a payroll-technology consultancy. He later ran regional sales operations before becoming chairman and chief executive. He studied industrial and organisational psychology at John Carroll University and completed management training at Harvard.",
    "html": "<p>Thomas F. Lozick leads Swagelok, the Ohio fluid-systems manufacturer founded by his grandfather, Fred Lennon. Before joining the family business, he owned a payroll-technology consultancy. He later ran regional sales operations before becoming chairman and chief executive. He studied industrial and organisational psychology at John Carroll University and completed management training at Harvard.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 53,
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
