  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "At the start of the pandemic, Swagelok chief executive Thomas Lozick explained how the manufacturer planned to keep supplying customers. A daily task force coordinated decisions, while the company used multiple raw-material suppliers, monitored inventories and arranged alternative transport. Local distributors were asked to maintain stocks of critical parts.\n\nAt the opening of Swagelok’s new headquarters in Solon, he emphasised the value of bringing people together. The building connected an innovation laboratory and customer collaboration centre directly to the main plant. A makerspace in the renovated factory gave employees somewhere to develop ideas alongside production work.",
    "html": "<p>At the start of the pandemic, Swagelok chief executive Thomas Lozick explained how the manufacturer planned to keep supplying customers. A daily task force coordinated decisions, while the company used multiple raw-material suppliers, monitored inventories and arranged alternative transport. Local distributors were asked to maintain stocks of critical parts.</p>\r\n<p>At the opening of Swagelok’s new headquarters in Solon, he emphasised the value of bringing people together. The building connected an innovation laboratory and customer collaboration centre directly to the main plant. A makerspace in the renovated factory gave employees somewhere to develop ideas alongside production work.</p>\r\n",
